homelab-calendar (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reminders (post-cutover #79): one email reminder per event, minutes
    before each occurrence (new events start at 10), to the owner and to
    everyone the calendar or event is shared with; each account may list
    where its reminders go (Settings; default its own address). A "Share
    with" field on new events takes one address (browser email check plus
    the server's). Migration 004: reminders, reminder_addresses and a
    reminder_queue drained by a runner in every hypnotoad worker through
    mailer: (calendar-orchestrate.sh --mailer copies drive's block).
  * Proposals at arrival (#80): with a third consent, email that looks like
    it carries an event is proposed by the AI service within a minute of
    arriving, without blocking; the proposal (and, for an entitled account
    with the switch on, the research facts) waits on the link's row, in a
    Suggestions list (Save / Open / Dismiss) and behind the email's link.
    Entitlements: PUT /internal/v1/calendar/admin/accounts/:email/entitlements
    (site_admin, through the api gateway).

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Sat, 15 Nov 2026 00:30:00 -0600

homelab-calendar (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * "Find out more" (post-cutover #78): the AI proposal now says whether a
